course: dictionary
lesson: 362
title: Antibiotics and bacteria
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Antibiotics are medicines that kill bacteria or stop them from multiplying, which means making more copies of themselves. Doctors use them to treat some infections caused by bacteria, such as some ear or chest infections.
explain: Antibiotics do not work on viruses. «Antibiotics kill bacteria, not viruses, so they do not help a cold.» A cold is caused by a virus, so an antibiotic cannot cure it, even though the medicine is strong.
explain: You must take antibiotics exactly as the doctor says. «A course of antibiotics should be finished as the doctor says, even when you feel better, because some bacteria may still be alive.» Stopping early can let the bacteria come back.
fact: Bacteria are tiny living things. Some are harmless, but some cause infections.
fact: Viruses are different from bacteria, and antibiotics do not work on them.
fact: «Antibiotics» means medicines that kill bacteria or stop them multiplying.
fact: Taking antibiotics when you do not need them helps bacteria become resistant, so the medicines stop working.
fact: The first antibiotic, penicillin, was discovered by Alexander Fleming from a mould.
exercise: «Antibiotics kill bacteria or stop them multiplying.» Find and copy the word that means making more copies. | effect | *multiplying | bacteria | kill
exercise: «Antibiotics kill bacteria, not viruses, so they do not help a cold.» What does this tell you? | Antibiotics will cure a cold in one day | A cold is caused by bacteria | *Antibiotics will not help a cold | Colds need a stronger dose
exercise: «A boy in Leeds did not clean a graze from the playground; two days later it was red, hot and full of pus, and he needed antibiotics.» Why did he need antibiotics? | *The graze became infected by bacteria | He had a cold | He fell off his bike | He ate too many sweets
test: Why might overusing antibiotics be a problem? | Antibiotics become tastier | Viruses are killed faster | *Bacteria can become resistant, so the medicines stop working | Doctors need fewer patients
test: Which illness would antibiotics not help? | A chest infection caused by bacteria | An infected graze caused by bacteria | An ear infection caused by bacteria | *A cold caused by a virus
exam: Mia has a cold and asks her doctor for antibiotics. What is the best answer? | *Antibiotics do not work on viruses, so they will not cure your cold | Yes, but only if you take them with milk | Yes, antibiotics will cure a cold quickly | Antibiotics only work on cats
